  "full_text": "I'm going to show you my first-person shooter and my flight simulator. They're done all the way from scratch, all the way down to bare metal, as I did myself. I don't use a GPU. This is using six cores to render. Looks kind of like shit, but... Anyway, now here's my first-person shooter. Let's go to... Here's my first-person shooter. This is the source code. It has graphics in my source code. There's the map, and here's some 3D graphics. I wrote my own compiler and graphics library. And look at this. There's a theta. You can use 8-bit characters instead of 7-bit. That was the stupidest thing, whoever thought of 7-bit ASCII instead of 8-bit. Anyway, so here's what it looks like. My first-person shooter. This is one core. I could use other cores. But that's a dilemma. What do you do with other cores? If you use them, what do you do? Like, I could have 8 times as much stuff. The only problem is, what if they're not available? How do you degrade your rendering or whatever? Anyway, so that's that.",
